      "q": "Are all the petals joined together or separate?",
      "a": "All the petals are separate, but joined together at bottom.\nClass 4 EVS Chapter 11 Question Answers Set 4\nHow is rose water used in your house? Is it used as medicine, sweets, lassi or something else? Find out and tell others.\nRose water is used as a medicine. It is also used to mix with sweets and lassi. Colours from Flowers.\nFind out and write the names of some more flowers that are used for making colours.\nRose and China Rose are used to make colours.\nCan you think of a colour of which there is no flower?\nI think there are no flowers which have silver colour.\nWrite the names of such flowers which are used to make scents.\nRose, jasmine, lavender and many other flowers are used to make scents.\nHave you ever read or heard any songs about flowers?\nThere are so many songs about flowers.\nDo you know when such songs are sung?\nDuring marriage.\nDo you or anybody else at home know other such songs?\nYes, my mother and grandmother know such songs.\nWhat are the different flowers that they sell? Ask them the names of three flowers.\nThey sell Rose, Jasmine, dahelia.\nClass 4 EVS Chapter 11 Question Answers Set 5\nWhere do they bring these flowers from?\nThey bring these flowers from gardens and horticulture farms.\nWhy do people buy flowers?\nPeople buy flowers for decoration, worship and to gift them.\nIn what forms do flower-sellers sell their flowers?\nflower-sellers sell their flowers in the form of loose flower, garland, Bouquet etc.\nHave you seen flowers offered at many religious places?\nYes.\nWhat do we do when they dry up?\nDried flowers are usually thrown away as waste.\nHow will you use them?\nI will use these flowers to make dry colours for Holi festival.\nFind out the prices of these different forms.  One flower,  One garland,  One bouquet\nPrices of different forms in which flowers are sold are as follows:\nOne flower \tRs. 10\nOne garland \tRs. 50\nOne bouquet\tRs. 200\nHas the flower-seller learnt to make bouquets or a net of flowers from anybody? From whom?\nYes, he has learnt to make bouquets or a net of flowers from his father.\nWould they like the other members of their family to do this work? Why?\nYes, they would like the other members of their family to do this work to make some extra earning."
