      "a": "Yes, I like it.\nClass 4 EVS Chapter 25 Question Answers Set 3\nSmall and round like a pearl, I am black when I am whole. I can be powdered coarse or fine A sharp and spicy taste is mine, Wheither it is salty or sweet I am added as a special treat, Think and tell me who am I? Tell me quickly, who am I?\nBlack pepper\nI am a small and skinny chap Sometimes I am brown and sometime black, added to hot oil and ghee I spread my fragrance all around me, When I am roasted. Curd and jaljeera are favourite to me. Think and tell me who am I? Tell me quickly, who am I?\nCinamon\nI look like Zeera though green am I, to make your stomach healthy I always try, eat me always after your meal I refresh your mouth, you surely feel, Think and tell me who am I? Tell me quickly, who am I?\nFennel seeds\nI look like a nail but a bud am I, Chocolate brown colour and a strong smell have I. When your toothache makes you shout, I soothe the pain in your mouth. Think and tell me who am I? Tell me quickly, who am I?\nClove\nQ1\nSpices are added to the food to:\n[A].\nenhance flavor,\n[B].\nadd colour of the food\n[C].\nmake the food tasty\n[D].\nAll of them\nAnswer: Option D\nExplanation:\nSpices serve several purposes in cooking and can be used to add flavor and aroma. They can change the taste of a meal by adding a range of flavors, enhance taste of food, change or enhance colour of the food.\nView Answer\nQ2\nRed Chilli is an important spice that:\n[A].\nis used in fruits\n[B].\nis put in milk\n[C].\nis put in vegetables, soups etc\n[D].\nnone of the above\nAnswer: Option C\nExplanation:\nChili powder is a staple spice used in all most all the kitchens, and has a lot of flavour. It\u2019s added to vegetables when being cooked, soups, stews, chili (of course), and a variety of dishes.\nView Answer\nQ3\nThis spice is good for pain in teeth and is made from flower bud:\n[A].\nturmeric\n[B].\nclove\n[C].\ncumin\n[D].\nall of these\nAnswer: Option B\nExplanation:\nCloves can be used whole or ground. People often include ground cloves in spice mixes and whole cloves in recipes to add flavour to a wide variety of foods. These small dark brown pods are used to spice up curries, season meats, enrich sauces. Cloves also have natural painkilling and antibacterial properties. They are used in Indian medicine where they have been as a cure for all sorts of aches and pains. Cloves are especially effective for the treatment of toothaches.\nView Answer\nQ4\nTurmeric is very used for:\n[A].\ncooking\n[B].\nskin cream\n[C].\nhealing an injury or sprain\n[D].\nall of them\nAnswer: Option D\nExplanation:\nIn India, turmeric is habitually used for disorders of the skin, upper respiratory tract, joints, and digestive system. Today, turmeric is also promoted as a dietary supplement for a variety of conditions, including arthritis, digestive disorders, respiratory infections, allergies, liver disease, depression, and many others.\nView Answer\nQ5\nWhat is Garam Masala?\n[A].\na mixture of spices added in fruits\n[B].\na mixture of spices added in milk\n[C].\na mixture of spices added to vegetables\n[D].\nnone of the above\nAnswer: Option C\nExplanation:\nGaram Masala is a powder of a mixture of several spices like cardamom (small and big), clove, cumin seeds (zeera) cinnamon which are added to the vegetables when they are cooked and ready to be served or eaten.\nView Answer\nQ6\nBlack pepper is grown in: hot and humid climate ii.red laterite soil iii. none of them iv. all of them\n[A].\na.\tBoth i and ii\n[B].\nBoth ii and iii\n[C].\nBoth i and iii\n[D].\nOnly iv\nAnswer: Option B\nExplanation:\nBlack pepper grows in hot and humid climates where the temperature never falls below 60 F (16 C). Black pepper can be grown in a wide range of soil though in its natural habitat it thrives well in red laterite soils.\nView Answer\nQ7\nTejpatta is also called:\n[A].\nCumin\n[B].\nCardamom\n[C].\nBayleaf\n[D].\nnone of the above\nAnswer: Option C\nExplanation:\nTejpatta or Indian Bayleaf helps to manage high cholesterol due to its antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties. It lowers the level of total blood cholesterol; bad cholesterol The heart-healthy fats present in Tejpatta also improves the level of good cholesterol. Bay leaves are a rich source of vitamin A, vitamin C, iron, potassium, calcium, and magnesium.\nView Answer\nQ8\nPotato chaat is made by using the following ingredients:\n[A].\npotato pieces\n[B].\nspices to add taste and flavour\n[C].\ncoriander leaves\n[D].\nall of these\nAnswer: Option D\nExplanation:\nThe recipe of making a potato chaat is to peel the boiled potatoes and cut them into small pieces. Then we add salt, red chilli powder, mango powder or lemon juice to it according to taste. To make the chaat more delicious, we add a little roasted cumin seeds, black salt and coriander powder. A pinch of garam masala is also added at the end. The potatoes are mixed well. Then we sprinkle chopped coriander leaves on top.\nView Answer"
