      "q": "If you were Abdul what would you have done?",
      "a": "I also did same thing as Abdul did.\nQ5\nChuskit was happy to see the wheel chair because:\n[A].\nshe could play with eat\n[B].\nshe could sleep on it\n[C].\nshe could go anywhere on her own now\n[D].\nall of these\nAnswer: Option C\nExplanation:\nChuskit was happier when her father (Aaba-le) got a chair which had wheels. She quickly learnt how to sit in the chair and how to move it \u2013 back and forth. Chuskit was so happy now as she did not need her father to carry her everywhere. When she wanted to go out she would tell her mother to put her in the wheel chair. Now, she could come outside on her own. Chuskit would now sit on it and see the other children laughing and playing on\r\ntheir way to school every morning.\nView Answer\nQ6\nWho agreed with Abdul\u2019s thinking about how to get Chuskit to school?\n[A].\nThe children\n[B].\nThe Headmaster and teachers\n[C].\nChuskit\u2019s father\n[D].\nNone of these\nAnswer: Option B\nExplanation:\nWhen Abdul went back from Chuskit\u2019s house; he had started thinking of how to get Chuskit to school. He explained about Chuskit to the Headmaster and talked to the teachers till they agreed with his thoughts. Now everyone got together to work so that Chuskit\u2019s problem could be solved. They made a plan so that Chuskit could bring her wheel-chair by road to school.\nView Answer\nQ7\nChuskit used to do the following things the whole day:\n[A].\nsit on her bed\n[B].\nplay with herself\n[C].\nsit near the window and draw pictures.\n[D].\nnone of the above\nAnswer: Option C\nExplanation:\nAs Chuskit was a differently abled child, she has no legs and could not walk. So she used to sit near the window and draw pictures whole day. Her mother said that Chuskit made the best drawings.\nView Answer\nQ8\nChuskit\u2019s grandfather had tears in his eyes because:\n[A].\nhe was sad\n[B].\nhe was very happy\n[C].\nhe didn\u2019t want Chuskit to go to school\n[D].\nnone of the above\nAnswer: Option B\nExplanation:\nChuskit\u2019s grandfather had tears in his eyes because he was very happy for her as she would now be able to go to the school like other children and study. He also wanted her to go to school but due to her disability could not send her.\nView Answer\nQ9\nChildren with disabilities face difficulties in school due to:\n[A].\nlack of money\n[B].\ninability to reach the school\n[C].\ninability of getting admission\n[D].\nNone of the above\nAnswer: Option B\nExplanation:\nSome children with disabilities face difficulties due to lack of convenience, both in terms of physically unapproachable school buildings and inappropriate learning materials. discrimination and unfairness which prevents children with disabilities from getting education like normal children.\nView Answer\nQ10\nA ramp is required in a __________ where disabled children are there.\n[A].\nschool\n[B].\nplayground\n[C].\nparty hall\n[D].\nAll of them\nAnswer: Option A\nExplanation:\nRamps provide an alternative to stairs for wheelchair users, people with mobility issues and people with prams, bicycles and other wheeled items. In case there is a child coming to school on wheel chair, he/she can easily enter through the ramp with someone\u2019s help or on his/ her own.\nView Answer\nQ11\nRamps are built in hospitals entrances and on every floor to allow:\n[A].\nthe patients to enter if on wheel chair\n[B].\nthe children to play on ramps\n[C].\nthe people to sit there\n[D].\nnone of the above\nAnswer: Option A\nExplanation:\nRamps are built on hospital entrances so that people who are disabled, injured, operated or having some medical problem can use wheelchair and get comfortably in the hospital. The stairs are usually not comfortable for wheelchair users as other people have to lift the wheelchair in order to get in the hospital.\nView Answer\nQ12\nThe difficulties that one has to face if he/she cannot attend the school are:\n[A].\nhe/she remains uneducated for the whole life\n[B].\nhe/she cannot earn money to fulfil his/her needs\n[C].\nBoth i and ii\n[D].\nNone of them\nAnswer: Option C\nExplanation:\nIf a child is unable to go to school due to any of the reason like poverty, disability etc then that child is left behind for their whole life in comparison to the other children. He remains poor and is unable to even afford basic needs of life. People who lack education have trouble getting ahead in life, have worse health and are poorer than the well-educated.\nView Answer\nQ13\nWhere does Chuskit live?\n[A].\nLadakh\n[B].\nBhutan\n[C].\nPakistan\n[D].\nAfghanistan\nAnswer: Option C\nExplanation:\nChuskit lives in Skitpopul village of Ladakh which is a mountain desert. It is a high altitude desert.\nView Answer\nQ14\nA person one who cannot see is called \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2013\n[A].\nDeaf\n[B].\nBlind\n[C].\nDumb\n[D].\nLame\nAnswer: Option B\nExplanation:\nPeople who cannot see are called blind. These people see the world around them but can still learn to read by using the Braille script. Braille script is a script which has letters with raised dots in a set pattern and the blind people can feel the raised letter with their fingers and read what is written.\nView Answer\nQ15\nInternational Disability day is celebrated on \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026..every year.\n[A].\n8th August\n[B].\n3rd December\n[C].\n4th March\n[D].\n7th December\nAnswer: Option B\nExplanation:\nThis day is celebrated on 3rd December every year to promote an understanding of disability issues and gather together support for the dignity, rights and well-being of persons with disabilities.\nView Answer\nQ16\nThe visually impaired people or the blind people move around with the help of a:\n[A].\nstick using their other senses\n[B].\ncrutches\n[C].\nwheel chair\n[D].\nall of these\nAnswer: Option A\nExplanation:\nBlind and visually impaired people use other senses like sound, touch and smell to get used to their surroundings. They use a stick to find their way, move around or to cross the road etc. They have with low vision or no vision and may use their other senses to get around.\nView Answer"
